MISTAKES = [
 "Reading 'Vitamin-M' as a story about a real vitamin. The 'M' stands for <b>memory</b>; the story is humorous and affectionate and is told by a third-person narrator.",
 "Missing the irony: Mother worries that Grandpa may forget his way, but it is Mother who forgot <b>Grandpa's birthday</b>. Naming Ravi or Grandpa as the one needing Vitamin-M loses the mark.",
 "Describing Ravi's secret following as rude or cruel. He hides behind benches and trees because he is worried about Grandpa, so state the motive (concern) along with the action.",
 "Mixing the poem with the story: 'I Cannot Remember My Mother' is by <b>Rabindranath Tagore</b>; its mood is tender and wistful, and the shiuli flower and the tune bring only a faint memory.",
 'Writing that the speaker of the poem hates or has forgotten his mother. He <i>cannot remember</i> her because she is no longer with him, so the feeling is loss, not anger.',
 "Tense errors: <i>Grandpa <b>had gone</b> out without telling anyone</i> (past perfect), not 'had went'. Plural of child is <i>children</i>.",
]
